 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532936,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the lengths of the missing sides in the given figure.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/38ba0fa8f72bb11c.png\" alt=\"A ray is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The ray lies in the first quadrant and a vertical dashed line is extended from a point on the ray to meet the x-axis and it makes a right angle. The horizontal distance from the origin to the line is marked 5. The angle made by the ray with the x-axis is marked 40 degrees. The distance from the origin to the point along the ray is labeled r.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find <i>y.</i></p>\n<p>The tangent of an angle is the opposite divided by the adjacent side: <span data-math=\"\\tan 40^\\circ = \\frac{{{\\text{opp}}}}{{{\\text{adj}}}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\tan 40^\\circ = \\frac{{\\text{y}}}{{\\text{5}}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y = 5\\tan 40^\\circ \\approx 4.2\"></span></p>\n<p>Find <i>r.</i></p>\n<p>The cosine of an angle is the adjacent side divided by the hypotenuse: <span data-math=\"\\cos 40^\\circ = \\frac{{{\\text{adj}}}}{{{\\text{hyp}}}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\cos 40^\\circ = \\frac{{\\text{5}}}{r}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"r\\cos 40^\\circ = 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"r = \\frac{5}{{\\cos 40^\\circ }} \\approx 6.53\"></span></p>\n<p>Note: You could have used the Pythagorean Theorem to find the second side. You can also use the Pythagorean Theorem to check your work. That is left to you.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {r = 6.53} \\\\ \n  {y = 4.2} \n\\end{array}\">\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {r = 6.53} \\\\ \n  {y = 4.2} \n\\end{array}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
